  "foaf:name": "Project 19",
  "sdo:name": "Project 19",
  "sdo:description": "Project 19 tackles ocean misinformation by empowering teens (15-18) to translate complex research into creative projects. Students analyze real science papers on ocean issues, then decide what&#x27;s important and how to share it through art, performances, or activities. Adults supervise but don&#x27;t influence their choices. Launched in Portugal (2021/22), Project 19 expands to South Africa (2024) and seeks EU funding for a European edition (2024/25). This hands-on approach builds ocean literacy and communication skills, turning teens into informed ocean advocates.",
  "sdo:location": "Portugal",
  "sdo:identifier": "77.7",
